desc: Harris Tweed (SWH plugins port) by chmaha
author: chmaha
version: 1.1
changelog:
  Add full copyright and licence header (upstream authors' notices).
tags: modular rack effects routing swh
about:
  Harris Tweed: a modular rack for 106 of Steve Harris's SWH audio plugins. Insert up to eight modules as
  blocks and patch them with cables between their input and output jacks, from IN (track channels 1/2, plus 3/4 as
  sidechain) to OUT. An output can feed any number of inputs and an input sums every cable plugged into it, so serial
  chains, parallel blends, sidechains and modulation patches are all possible. A fresh rack passes the input straight
  through.
  Right-click the canvas (or use ADD MODULE) to insert a module after the selected block, or before OUT when nothing is
  selected (hold Shift to insert it unpatched). Mono modules take the left signal and feed both sides. Drag between an
  output jack and an input jack, in either direction, to add a cable; pull a cable well away from its path and release
  to unplug it. Right-click cables, jacks or blocks to disconnect, bypass, remove or reset. Delete removes the selected
  block. CABLE SLACK sets how loosely the cables hang.
  The rack processes in fixed blocks of 128 samples and reports 128 samples plus the longest module latency path to
  REAPER for compensation. Requires REAPER 7 or later (more than 64 sliders).
  Ported from Steve Harris's swh-plugins, https://github.com/swh/lv2 (GPL-3). Upstream bugs fixed in this version:
  Reverse Delay always 1 sample long; out-of-table reads in the Surround Encoder and Bode Shifter CV;
  flanger and retro flanger blow-ups; multivoice chorus overflow; Transient mangler and GVerb out-of-bounds reads at
  high sample rates; GVerb frozen at damping 1; lookahead limiter overshoot (output clip enabled); Fast Lookahead
  limiter block-size dependence; SE4 muting at ratio 1; Dyson NaN at release 0; Satan Maximiser NaN on silence;
  sine oscillator frequency clamp; wave shaper negative shapes; delay line wrap glitches; VyNil stuck clicks at 70/78
  rpm; Multiband EQ gain error and latency report; Pitch Scaler dropping half the spectrum; GSM input wrap; DJ EQ false
  latency; plate reverb damping (cut the lows, not the highs) and size at high sample rates; gong beater strike
  reset; uninitialised state in Chebstortion and Offset.
  GVerb by Juhana Sadeharju (GPL-2+). GSM 06.10 codec by Jutta Degener and Carsten Bormann, Technische Universitaet
  Berlin (see Dependencies/HarrisTweed/GSM-COPYRIGHT.txt). Impulse convolver: impulses 1-3 captured by Steve Harris;
  impulses 4-21 (Fender, Marshall and Matchless cabinets) were collected by someone else whose name and origin are
  unknown, as Steve notes.
  JSFX version released under GPLv3 license
  Claude generated some of this code
provides:
  Dependencies/HarrisTweed/swh_dsp.jsfx-inc
  Dependencies/HarrisTweed/GSM-COPYRIGHT.txt
